  you still want to train your upper body  one of the best ways to do this is by  using resistance machine what's more  though you can use resistance machines  to gently and safely rehab a injured  joint or muscle and I have first-hand  experience of this I haven't talked much  on this channel about this but I went  through a period of about two years  where I had a bad knee it hurt me when I  ran when I squatted and did all kinds of  other things and it's now completely  gone after two years of thinking this  was just going to be it from now on to  chronic pain I managed to completely get  rid of it and there are a few things  that helped with this but probably one  of the things that helped the most was  just doing really light leg extensions  it should never work for pain but if  you're able to move the injured site  gently this is a great way to get blood  flowing to encourage healing and  recovery and to strengthen the muscles  and to improve movement patterns and  that's exactly what I was able to do but  I did say that I also think resistance  machines have their place more broadly  for anybody who wants to build  impressive strength and I think they can  be one of the most effective and  Powerful tools for building max strength  those of you who watch channel regularly  will know that I'm not just interested  in building strength I'm interested in  human performance across the board and  that includes things like productivity  and cognitive performance and for that  endel today's sponsor is an absolutely  fantastic tool so Wendell is an app and  what it does is it creates personalized  atmospheric soundscapes that can react  to inputs like location weather even  your heart rate if you have a compatible  smart watch this one's really cool  because it actually uses gyroscopes to  respond to the way you're moving it's  called move  these Landscapes can fit a variety of  scenarios they're perfect if you're  trying to be productive but you can also  listen to them when you're unwinding  meditating or trying to Drift Off to  Sleep the app is based on no  neuroscience and it's been shown to  boost productivity more efficiently than  listening to your Spotify playlist for  instance on top of that there are  special content Partnerships with a  range of cool and original artists the  app has these really nice visualizations  as well which I actually find Aid with  that productive mindset if you want to  check it out yourself then the first 100  people to download envelope at the link  below will get a free week of audio  experiences thank you once again to  endel for sponsoring today's video and  now on with the show  but I did say that I also think  resistance machines have their place  more broadly for anybody who wants to  build impressive strength and I think  they can be one of the most effective  and Powerful tools for building max  strength the obvious reason for this is  that you can safely pile on a huge  amount of weight you can challenge  yourself to lift something you wouldn't  be able to do without a very good  Spotter and even then it's a little bit  you know hairy I used to do crazy bench  presses with my friend who'd spot me but  these days I don't necessarily have  someone strong enough to stand behind me  and I know that they're going to be able  to lift that 150 kilograms off of me if  I get trapped underneath in fact I  usually train alone and I don't  particularly like asking strangers to  help spot me so I avoid my one rep max  and I avoid my two rep max and my three  rep max and instead I do things I can do  for maybe four repetitions and then I  usually stop short of complete failure  because obviously I don't get pinned  underneath that's extremely embarrassing  and it can also strangle you even worse  for something like the squat or the  deadlift where you risk injuring your  back or getting trapped you know  underneath at the bottom of the squat  there are things you can do with pins  but there's still that element of risk  you can even just twist your body tip  the weight find it's a little bit  unbalanced conversely if you're on a  chest press if you're on a leg press or  something like that you can put as much  weight as you like on there if you can't  lift it no problem also not that  embarrassing because no one can really  see what you're doing and if you do get  stuck you can just drop it it'll make a  loud crash but it won't go anywhere and  it's not going to hurt anyone far far  safer this means you can not only train  with your one rep max but you can really  push and push and go beyond that and  this is important because when you lift  a one rep maximum you actually aren't  performing a one rep max very long at  all the one at Max as an exercise takes  you know a few seconds but even within  those few seconds only a very small  portion of that is truly your maximum  effort because of the strength curve  because of the leverage because of joint  angles because of momentum so for  example there's going to be a sticking  point in the squat for many people it's  down the bottom that's the hardest part  for them so that's the only point at  which they're providing their maximum  effort so we're talking a fraction of a  second and you can't go higher than that  you can use things like accommodating  resistance etc etc and that's obviously  an option but even then it's not precise  science conversely you can load your one  rep max and you can hold that sticking  point you can try and fight it and then  as soon as you're done you can lower the  weight slightly and go again so that you  really are providing your maximum effort  for a much longer duration of time and  this is important because not only are  you causing maximum muscle damage for  potential growth but also training that  neural Drive the ability to engage that  maximum strength and this is what's  really key here so by doing that you're  teaching your body to recruit more motor  units and thereby 